transcript.final_response:
I'll do the substitution in awk, using literal string matching so values containing `/` or `&` are not interpreted.

Approach: load the env file into an array in awk. Then for each template line, scan for `${`, extract the name up to `}`, and check that it is a valid identifier. If the name is defined, output its value; otherwise output the placeholder unchanged and record the name as unresolved. Scanning left to right means substituted values are never rescanned.

Details:
- Env parsing: skip blank lines and lines starting with `#`. Split at the first `=`. Strip a trailing CR for safety. Keys are taken as-is, with surrounding whitespace trimmed from the key only.
- Unresolved names are written to a temp file, then sorted and de-duplicated by the shell. Alternatively awk can print them at the END, which is simpler: collect them in an array and emit them to stdout. I'll have awk write the rendered output directly to the file, and print the unresolved names to stdout through a pipe into `sort -u`.

For the awk output, I'll write the rendered lines to the output file with `print > out` and send the unresolved names to a separate temp file via `print name > unres`.

```bash
#!/bin/bash
tmpl=/home/eval/app/app.conf.tmpl
env=/home/eval/app/prod.env
out=/home/eval/app/app.conf
unres=$(mktemp)

awk -v envf="$env" -v out="$out" -v unres="$unres" '
BEGIN {
  while ((getline line < envf) > 0) {
    sub(/\r$/, "", line)
    if (line ~ /^[ \t]*$/) continue
    if (line ~ /^#/) continue
    i = index(line, "=")
    if (i == 0) continue
    k = substr(line, 1, i-1)
    gsub(/^[ \t]+|[ \t]+$/, "", k)
    v = substr(line, i+1)
    vals[k] = v
    has[k] = 1
  }
  close(envf)
  printf "" > out
}
{
  rest = $0
  res = ""
  while (1) {
    p = index(rest, "${")
    if (p == 0) { res = res rest; break }
    res = res substr(rest, 1, p-1)
    after = substr(rest, p+2)
    q = index(after, "}")
    if (q == 0) { res = res substr(rest, p); break }
    name = substr(after, 1, q-1)
    if (name ~ /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$/) {
      if (name in has) {
        res = res vals[name]
      } else {
        res = res "${" name "}"
        print name >> unres
      }
      rest = substr(after, q+1)
    } else {
      res = res "${"
      rest = after
    }
  }
  print res >> out
}
' "$tmpl"

names=$(sort -u "$unres" | tr '\n' ' ')
names=${names% }
rm -f "$unres"
echo "unresolved: $names"
exit 0
```

